{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And these are the garments.</b> It mentions first the hoshen, which is above the ephod, which is above the robe, and afterward the tunic and the sash that girds him and the turban on his head, and so it was when Aaron washed in water and put on linen breeches — and there is no need to mention them now, nor at the time of the act, for it is every person's practice to put on breeches. Now Moses put the tunic on him, and afterward placed the turban on his head and placed on the turban the frontlet of the holy diadem, and it did not mention in this verse — though it is counting the priestly garments — the frontlet of the holy diadem, for it is not a garment. Our predecessors mentioned it on account of the many who count the priestly garments. And the Urim and Tummim are not garments, nor stones, nor parchments. And afterward he girded him with the sash, and afterward he put the robe on him, and after that the ephod, and he fastened it on him with it, for the hoshen is part of the ephod, and on account of the hoshen it is called ephod. And behold, this follows the order that is in this verse. And do not be astonished that you find written last in the account of the act, 'and he placed the turban on his head' (Leviticus 8:9) — for its meaning is: he had already placed the turban with the golden frontlet when he put on the tunic; and like it, 'and they clothed him with garments' (Zechariah 3:5), and they had already clothed him, for at first it is written, 'and they placed the pure turban on his head' (ibid.)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:38:50.108901236Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}